ggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":0,\"duplicates\":32,\"reachDelta1d\":null,\"reachDelta7d\":null,\"reachDelta30d\":0},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"AU\",\"CA\",\"GB\",\"NZ\",\"SG\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":9,\"currentRank\":9,\"rankDelta\":null,\"improvementPct\":3.41},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":true,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1124029566688457\",\"collationId\":\"1486424536675126\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-05T02:36:16.155Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-11-02T08:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-27T02:15:50.883Z\",\"daysRunning\":25,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/af6e2385e23ebb657098e75bcda12c68d1269d5f48bf4671fc85ba38e5514186.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/cb9fc49ccc8b42c18b8365ffc94783c5cff6f5c436e88c773ab0b8358c67808b.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1106647162524028\",\"name\":\"Blood Sugar Balance Community\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1106647162524028.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1106647162524028\",\"liveAdsCount\":4312,\"reach30d\":1892898,\"totalReach\":3974228,\"countriesCount\":2,\"facebookLikes\":7770,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Looking to Support Healthy Blood Sugar Naturally? 🌿\\n\\nExperience the Power of Metabolae Sri Lankan Ceylon Cinnamon!\\n\\n✅ Helps support healthy blood sugar levels\\n✅ Supports steady daily energy\\n✅ Helps reduce blood sugar crashes\\n✅ Authentic Sri Lankan Ceylon cinnamon\\n✅ 200+ Clinical studies\\n✅ Enhanced with MCT oil for absorption\\n\\nSupport healthier glucose metabolism naturally with research-backed ingredients designed for daily stability.\",\"transcript\":\"Public apology to every Metabolé customer. I lied. Now I have to make it right. I told you that was the best price you'd ever get and then we overproduced. We made too much. Yes, we seriously overproduced. This is the last chance to get the best sale we have ever had on our website. Go take full advantage of our sale and the buy two, get one free offer plus free shipping right now. Because once this overstock is gone, it's gone. This is the last chance. You're not going to find a deal like this for a very long time. You're not going to find a deal.\",\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://metabolae.com/products/softgels-ceylon\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"metabolae.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg Equivalent with MCT Oil\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":9012,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":81,\"duplicates\":31,\"reachDelta1d\":443,\"reachDelta7d\":3511,\"reachDelta30d\":8969},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"GB\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":146,\"currentRank\":146,\"rankDelta\":2,\"improvementPct\":3.39},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1462997231934051\",\"collationId\":\"1968638653753176\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"inactive\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-04-09T02:19:24.413Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-04-08T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-07-07T07:00:00.000Z\",\"daysRunning\":90,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/ec37c93f225af74204b5725f5dc79f75f07bf973385802b9c51825be3694b322.jpg\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"895238260349097\",\"name\":\"Diabetes reserve for Beginners\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/895238260349097.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"895238260349097\",\"liveAdsCount\":0,\"reach30d\":0,\"totalReach\":7125,\"countriesCount\":14,\"facebookLikes\":53,\"instagramFollowers\":34},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Tried berberine before and it either wrecked your stomach or did absolutely nothing? 🫠\\n\\nNot your fault. Not the ingredient. The delivery.\\n\\nCapsules take 45 minutes to dissolve. ⏱️\\nYour blood sugar spikes 15 minutes after eating. 📈\\n\\nThe capsule never had a chance. And your gut paid the price for it getting nowhere near the problem.\\n\\nGLUCO GONE is liquid. Sublingual. Under your tongue.\\n\\n90 seconds → bloodstream → liver. Before the spike starts. Zero gut destruction. Zero waiting.\\n\\nAnd it's not just berberine. 12 ingredients working together 👇\\n\\n🌿 Berberine — clinically shown to support healthy glucose metabolism\\n🌿 Gymnema — blocks sugar receptors. Cravings gone.\\n🌿 Ceylon Cinnamon — insulin sensitivity support\\n🌿 Bitter Melon + Chromium + Turmeric — multi-pathway glucose control\\n\\nWhat Ozempic does for $1,200 a month — naturally. No prescription. No injection. No side effects. 💉❌\\n\\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ 1,503+ women. A1C dropping. Cravings quieting. Weight following.\\n\\n90-day guarantee. You keep the bottle either way.\\n\\n👇 Try the formula that actually reaches your liver.\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://try-elixir.co/pages/tryelixir-ac1-2025-12-23-02-36-37-pm\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"try-elixir.co\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Finally. A Blood Sugar Drop That Doesn't Destroy Your Gut.\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":\"You Don't Fight Cravings With This. They Just Stop.\"},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":null,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":null,\"duplicates\":31,\"reachDelta1d\":null,\"reachDelta7d\":null,\"reachDelta30d\":null},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"AU\",\"BR\",\"CA\",\"DE\",\"DK\",\"GB\",\"HK\",\"JP\",\"MX\",\"NZ\",\"PH\",\"PL\",\"SG\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"DK\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":null,\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":true,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1699359537941807\",\"collationId\":\"1022233100711673\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-29T21:45:04.195Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-07-28T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-08-01T20:40:58.280Z\",\"daysRunning\":122,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/9ac4d623305b8e5abfcf0079ea95ca652c1f81e2892eece17f38b9c6a0b7a869.png\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1018883361310799\",\"name\":\"Sandra Keller, RN\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1018883361310799.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1018883361310799\",\"liveAdsCount\":585,\"reach30d\":657004,\"totalReach\":4231542,\"countriesCount\":5,\"facebookLikes\":40683,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"The best way to protect your kidneys is NOT drinking more water, NOT cutting protein, and definitely NOT waiting for dialysis. If your doctor has mentioned protein in your urine, rising creatinine, or declining kidney function — you need to hear this. What they don't tell you is what comes next.\\n\\nI used to ask every new dialysis patient the same thing: \\\"What was your A1C before your kidneys failed?\\\" After 11,000 patients and the same answer every single time, I stopped asking. It was always \\\"managed.\\\" Always between 6.5 and 7.5. Always someone who'd been told to cut protein, reduce salt, and come back in six months. The chairs aren't full of people who ignored their kidneys. They're full of people who trusted the wrong number.\\n\\nI'm telling you this now because last month I got my own prediabetes diagnosis with creeping creatinine — and I refuse to end up in one of my own chairs.\\n\\nI'm a dialysis nurse. Fourteen years. Roughly 11,000 patients connected to machines. Let me tell you what that actually looks like.\\n\\nThe slow, irreversible slide. 10%. Then 20%. Then 50%. Until one day your doctor says: \\\"You need dialysis. Three times a week. Four hours per session. For the rest of your life.\\\"\\n\\nA needle goes into a fistula — a surgical access point in the arm that leaves a scar most patients hide under long sleeves even in summer.\\n\\nThen comes the exhaustion. Not normal tiredness. The kind where you can barely lift your head off the pillow. Your body is poisoning itself with waste your kidneys can't filter anymore.\\n\\nThe swelling in your legs, ankles, and face. Puffiness that makes you unrecognizable to your own grandchildren.\\n\\nThe dietary restrictions that make eating miserable. No potassium. No phosphorus. No salt. Bananas dangerous. Tomatoes dangerous. Cheese dangerous.\\n\\nAnd the waiting list. Years. Sometimes a decade. Praying for a transplant that might never come.\\n\\nI've watched marriages buckle under the schedule. I've watched grandchildren learn to plan around Grandma's dialysis days. I've watched a 61-year-old man read the same magazine in the waiting room every Tuesday and Thursday for three years while his wife was connected.\\n\\nI've watched patients stop coming. I know what that means.\\n\\nOne of my long-term patients — Ruth, 63, three years in my unit — told me something I think about every day. She said: \\\"This isn't living. This is just not dying yet.\\\"\\n\\nEvery. Single. One.\\n\\nSo here's the trap most people are stuck in. Two paths. Both lead to suffering.\\n\\nPath one: Follow doctor's orders. Cut protein. Drink more water. Take the ACE inhibitor. Monitor labs every six months. Watch your kidney function drop year after year anyway.\\n\\nPath two: Do nothing. Leave the damage unchecked. Foam in the toilet that won't go away. Ankles that swell by 4 PM. Crushing fatigue that won't lift no matter how much you rest.\\n\\nMost people over the age of 50 tragically ignore these symptoms until it's too late. They blame the puffiness on age. They blame the fatigue on stress. They blame the foam on hard water.\\n\\nIt's none of those things. It's your kidneys screaming for help.\\n\\nBut there's a third path your doctor will never mention. And it's the only one I've ever seen actually move the numbers in the right direction.\\n\\nLast month I sat in my own doctor's office and heard \\\"prediabetes\\\" attached to my own name.\\n\\nA1C: 6.4. Fasting glucose 135 to 145.\\n\\nAnd here's the part that made my hands go cold — my creatinine had crept from 0.8 to 1.0 over ten months. My GFR had dropped from 98 to 86. There was foam in my toilet most mornings. My ankles were swelling by 4 PM. The fatigue I'd been blaming on long shifts wasn't from the shifts.\\n\\nOn paper, none of that was alarming. My doctor said \\\"we'll keep an eye on it.\\\"\\n\\nBut I've heard those exact words from the charts of people now sitting in my chairs.\\n\\nI know what a creatinine of 1.0 looks like at the BEGINNING. Because I've held the hands of people whose creatinine started at 1.0.\\n\\nI felt something I'd never felt in 14 years of nursing — real, bone-deep terror. Not for my patients. For myself.\\n\\nSo I stopped trusting the monitoring and started asking a different question. Not \\\"how do I slow this down\\\" — but \\\"why is my body actually doing this in the first place?\\\"\\n\\nHere's what nobody explains to you.\\n\\nThink of every cell in your body like a tiny room. On the walls there are doors — small protein doors called GLUT4 transporters. In a healthy body those doors stay open. Sugar comes through the blood, doors open, sugar goes inside, cell burns it for energy.\\n\\nIn an insulin-resistant body, those doors retreat. They pull away from the wall. The pancreas sends the signal — and they don't answer.\\n\\nSo sugar piles up in the blood. The doors are shut.\\n\\nThat sugar doesn't just wait there. It destroys things.\\n\\nThink of your kidneys like the finest mesh screen — millions of tiny filters called glomeruli. That excess sugar is like sand being forced through the mesh under pressure.\\n\\nHour after hour. Day after day. The mesh starts to tear. First it leaks a little protein — that's the foam in the toilet most people are too scared to google.\\n\\nThen the tears get bigger. Then filtration drops. Then the system fails.\\n\\nAnd it's not just kidneys.\\n\\nThat same sugar pileup strips the insulation off your nerves — that's why your feet burn. It starves your brain — that's why the fog rolls in by 2pm. It wrecks the vessels behind your eyes — that's why the floaters showed up. It locks your body in fat-storage mode — that's why the belly won't budge. It shatters your sleep — that's why you're up three times a night. And it damages the blood vessels responsible for intimacy — that's why that part of your life quietly disappeared.\\n\\nALL of it traces back to the same closed doors.\\n\\nYour doctor monitors the headline number. The story underneath is your organs falling apart.\\n\\nNow let me address what you're probably thinking.\\n\\nFirst: \\\"What about cutting protein?\\\"\\n\\nCutting protein gives the torn mesh less to filter. It doesn't repair the mesh. It doesn't stop the sand. The tearing continues — quieter, but still happening.\\n\\nSecond: \\\"I've been drinking more water.\\\"\\n\\nDrinking more water flushes toxins. But it doesn't stop the friction tearing your filters. You're running more fluid through the same broken screens.\\n\\nThird: \\\"What about ACE inhibitors?\\\"\\n\\nACE inhibitors slow the damage by reducing pressure. But the sand is still coming. The mesh is still tearing. Just slower.\\n\\nAll of these target pieces of the puzzle — but miss the complete mechanism. The doors are still closed. The sugar is still piling up. The damage continues underneath whatever you're doing on top.\\n\\nThe monitoring just measures how torn the mesh is getting. Nobody is stopping the sand.\\n\\n—\\n\\nWhen I started pulling research on PubMed, I found compounds that may actually help coax those doors back open.\\n\\nType-A Polymers and MHCP. Found in one specific plant — Ceylon cinnamon. Cinnamomum verum.\\n\\nA 2003 study in Diabetes Care showed a 29% drop in fasting blood glucose. A 2012 review in the Journal of Medicinal Food analyzed eight randomized trials and found meaningful drops in fasting glucose and A1C. Research in Pharmacognosy Research mapped the GLUT4 mechanism — how these compounds bring those doors back to the surface.\\n\\nWhen the doors reopen, the sand stops being forced through the mesh. Protein leakage drops. Creatinine stabilizes. GFR holds.\\n\\nPublished. Proven. Replicated.\\n\\nAnd every time I bring this up with someone whose kidneys are declining, I get the look.\\n\\nWide eyes. Raised eyebrows.\\n\\nThat \\\"You mean… cinnamon? The thing in my pumpkin pie? That's supposed to fix my kidneys?\\\" face.\\n\\nI get it. It sounds unrelated.\\n\\nBut the people who come back to me eight weeks later always come back in tears. Their fasting numbers stabilized. Their creatinine stopped climbing. Some of their GFR numbers went up — which is supposed to be impossible without a transplant.\\n\\nTheir faces have changed. The puffiness is gone. They're sleeping. They look like themselves again for the first time in years.\\n\\nAnd many of them showed their doctors their new numbers and heard the words they never thought possible:\\n\\n\\\"Your kidney function is stable. Keep doing whatever you're doing.\\\"\\n\\nIn 14 years working in a dialysis unit — not one doctor has ever mentioned any of this to a patient in my care.\\n\\nNot because they're hiding it. Because the pipeline that moves research from a journal into a treatment room runs on patent money.\\n\\nYou can't patent a plant. No patent means no money. No sales reps, no training updates, no guideline changes.\\n\\nThat should make you angry. Not at your doctor. At the structure that kept this from all of us — including the nurse who works at the end of the road.\\n\\nAnd I understood instantly why every cinnamon supplement on every shelf had never worked for anyone. Three things wrong with all of them.\\n\\nWrong species. Most use Cassia — completely different plant. 250 times more coumarin, which can damage your liver at daily doses.\\n\\nWrong dose. A 500mg capsule is a taste-level dose. Studies used the equivalent of thousands of milligrams — concentrated and extracted.\\n\\nNo delivery system. The compounds that target those doors are fat-soluble. They need fat to cross a cell wall made of fat. A hard capsule full of dry powder can't carry them through.\\n\\nI've watched patients bring supplement bottles to dialysis sessions and ask if they should keep taking them. I look at the label — Cassia, 500mg, dry powder — and I don't know what to say. It's like bringing a garden hose to a house fire.\\n\\nIf you tried cinnamon before and it did nothing — you weren't wrong to try. The tool was wrong.\\n\\n—\\n\\nAfter I understood the mechanism and the delivery failure, I found something called Metabolae.\\n\\nReal Ceylon cinnamon — Cinnamomum verum — concentrated 12-to-1 into a liquid extract suspended in MCT oil. Then sealed inside a softgel.\\n\\nOne softgel a day delivers the equivalent of 7,200mg of raw Ceylon. The therapeutic range the studies used. Because the extract is already suspended in MCT oil, the moment the gel dissolves, the active compounds are riding the fat carrier they need. Not trapped in dry fiber. Suspended, bioavailable, ready to reach the cell.\\n\\nDNA-verified. Third-party tested for heavy metals every batch.\\n\\nSourced from Sri Lanka — the original home of true Ceylon cinnamon, where the tree has been cultivated for over two thousand years. The diabetes rate there sits far below America's close to 50 percent. The kidney failure rate is a fraction of ours.\\n\\nI work in a dialysis unit that's always full. In Sri Lanka, they barely need one.\\n\\nComes in a sealed bag, not a bottle stuffed with fillers.\\n\\nOne softgel. Swallow it with your morning coffee. That's it. No measuring. No mixing. No taste. It's the one part of the morning that doesn't feel like managing a disease.\\n\\nHere's what happened to me.\\n\\nWithin two weeks the fog lifted. Not managed — lifted. My feet stopped aching. The ankle swelling was gone by Friday of the second week. I slept through the night for the first time in months.\\n\\nBy week four my fasting readings — which had been running 135 to 145 — started showing up in the low 90s. The foam in the toilet was gone. I checked three mornings in a row to be sure.\\n\\nAt ten weeks I got my blood panel back.\\n\\nA1C: 6.4 to 5.4. Creatinine: back to 0.8. GFR: climbed from 86 to 94. Protein in the urine: undetectable. Seven pounds gone without changing what I ate.\\n\\nBut the thing I remember most isn't a number. It's my own doctor looking at the panel, then looking at me, and saying:\\n\\n\\\"Your kidney function is stable. Keep doing whatever you're doing.\\\"\\n\\nAnd then walking into my dialysis unit the next morning knowing — for the first time in months — I wasn't going to end up in one of my own chairs.\\n\\nI told Ruth what I'd found. She looked at me with tears running down her face and said:\\n\\n\\\"Tell everyone. Don't let them end up like me.\\\"\\n\\nThat's why I'm writing this.\\n\\nIn a recent customer survey, 78% of Metabolae users noticed more consistent readings within 30 days. 82% reported steadier energy. 74% said cravings loosened. 69% reported burning and tingling in their feet improved. 67% said their doctor commented on their bloodwork. Across 2,660+ verified reviews — 4.8 stars. Less than 1% have ever asked for their money back.\\n\\n—\\n\\nYou're in a window right now.\\n\\nThe monitoring phase — the \\\"we're keeping an eye on it\\\" phase — is the ONLY phase where the trajectory can still change. Every patient in my dialysis chairs was in that window once. Every one of them would give anything to go back to it.\\n\\nOne side — nothing changes. The creatinine climbs. The GFR drops. The foam shows up. The ankles puff up until your grandchildren don't recognize you. 10% drop. Then 20%. Then 50%.\\n\\nAnd one morning you're not reading about dialysis — you're being scheduled for it. Three days a week. Four hours a session. The fistula scar hidden under long sleeves. No potassium. No phosphorus. No salt. The transplant waiting list that may never come through.\\n\\nThe chair.\\n\\nThe other side…\\n\\nOne softgel. Swallowed with your morning coffee. Five seconds. Done.\\n\\nOver the next few weeks the energy holds. The fog lifts. The feet quiet. The swelling drops. The foam disappears.\\n\\nAnd at your next blood panel, your doctor looks up from the chart and says something you haven't heard in two years:\\n\\n\\\"Your kidney function is stable. Keep doing whatever you're doing.\\\"\\n\\nThe window stays open. The chair stays empty.\\n\\nRight now Metabolae has a deal — buy two bags, get one free. Three-month supply. The exact window the research points to for meaningful kidney marker and A1C changes. Six bags gets you free shipping plus a recipe guide and benefits booklet.\\n\\nHand-harvested, certified Ceylon from Sri Lanka. Concentrated 12-to-1. Suspended in MCT oil. Sealed in softgels. Not factory-produced Cassia powder pressed into hard capsules. Harvest cycles are limited. The next harvest has a lead time.\\n\\nEvery order comes with a 90-day money-back guarantee. If you're not genuinely amazed by the shift in your fasting readings, the foam that disappears, the ankles that go down, the feet that stop burning, the kidney labs trending the right direction — you get every dollar back.\\n\\nLess than 1% ever ask. That number says everything.\\n\\nThe doors are closed. The sand is still coming. But the window is still open.\\n\\nDon't let someone else tell your story with the words \\\"I wish someone had told me sooner.\\\"\\n\\nI just did.\\n\\nIf you're in the monitoring phase right now — the creeping creatinine, the dropping GFR, the foam in the toilet, the doctor \\\"keeping an eye on it\\\" — at least check out that page. It breaks down exactly how the Ceylon extract works and why the cinnamon you tried before didn't do anything.\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://metabolae.com/pages/pre-ins-3-kid\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"metabolae.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg Equivalent with MCT Oil\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":\"Metabolae\"},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":26109,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":235,\"duplicates\":28,\"reachDelta1d\":546,\"reachDelta7d\":5631,\"reachDelta30d\":24811},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"AU\",\"CA\",\"GB\",\"NZ\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":60,\"currentRank\":60,\"rankDelta\":2,\"improvementPct\":10.26},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":true,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1682001966862629\",\"collationId\":\"1643768477110318\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-09T02:49:03.328Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-10-07T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:23:22.359Z\",\"daysRunning\":51,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/3268f3bbe780ee0d9965577d23e7a4083ecffd44c17e1ef05bb260535870bd5d.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/a787643ba99a96f5198246bb4190faae65751688a45270810e95f0b0ded4a8d6.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"116565354374771\",\"name\":\"Blood Sugar Wellness\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/profile_picture/116565354374771.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"116565354374771\",\"liveAdsCount\":240,\"reach30d\":0,\"totalReach\":0,\"countriesCount\":1,\"facebookLikes\":2755,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Want to Support Healthy Blood Sugar — All Day Long? ❤️\\n\\nExperience the Power of Resilia Ceylon Cinnamon + Berberine!\\n\\n✅ Supports healthy blood sugar levels\\n✅ Supports healthy insulin response\\n✅ Supports healthy glucose metabolism\\n✅ Supports healthy post-meal blood sugar\\n✅ 1,000mg True Ceylon Cinnamon Extract\\n✅ Standardized for cinnamaldehyde & polyphenols\\n✅ Plus 500mg Berberine HCl\\n\\nSupport your metabolic health with two powerful ingredients working together — 30-Day Risk-Free Guarantee.\",\"transcript\":\"Dad, is that pasta your mother's best? First Sunday home in two months, and he starts with the meter. Hand, please. Always the same greeting. 104. Good number. It hasn't hit yet. Last time I checked you, you were still in the 100 and forties before dinner. Give it an hour. Then let us give it an hour. No. Dad, absolutely not. Eat your pasta, that's okay. I can't just sit here and watch you eat this. Then close your eyes. It's been an hour. Hand. Of course. 98. A good number. 101. 91. So the meter works. Uncle Sugar is fine too. How is this possible? You can ask me properly. Dad, how is this possible? Two months ago, you checked me at this table, still in the one hundred and forties. I took my pills every morning the way you made me promise. Nothing moved. And then? And then I did not call you. Why not? Because you would have told me to stop eating. He heard every word you said, you know? He just also wanted his pasta. Every Sunday for years, I have listened to you worry. I loved you for it. I just wanted my wife's cooking too. So who did you call? An old friend, Ono san. The spice man from the market? Forty years of Ceylon in that shop. You never asked him anything. Neither did I until I ran out of other places to ask. Tatsuo, you never come on a weekday. I did not come to buy tea. I take all my pills every morning exactly as I am told. My blood sugar keeps running high anyway. Dasuke checks me whenever he is home, and every time his face grows more tired than mine. And you came here instead of telling him? Because I know you have natural ways, Ono. I have heard the stories for years. Customers say you could tell them what to put in their tea for their knees, their sleep, their stomachs. Stories travel faster than spice. They tell us our people live longer than almost anyone in the world. I seem to have missed whatever it is. The old people here keep small daily habits, real food, walking, and a few things that came here by ship. Come. Let me show you something I sold for forty years. Cinnamon. Most people think there is only one kind. Sharp, almost bitter. Cassia. This one from China, this one from Vietnam. Cheap, mass produced, and what most of the world means when it says cinnamon. It does very little for your health. This is true Ceylon from Sri Lanka. Cinnaminum verum. They named it true so people would stop confusing it. Smell. That smells like my mother's kitchen. What is it for? Your insulin still works. Your cells stopped answering it. Cinnamon helps them answer again. Then I will chew it every morning. You would need a great deal of bark. And on its own, it only gets you halfway. It needs a partner. What partner? Wait. Even the smell is bitter. Berberine, a yellow powder from the roots of certain plants. My grandfather sold one of them as orein, gold thread. Bitter, yes, which is why it comes in a capsule now. It helps the cinnamon dissolve and reach your cells, and it activates AMPK, the switch that decides burn or store. Two ingredients, two halves of the same problem. And where do I find both done properly? A small American company, Resilia. Real Ceylon, real berberine tested by an outside lab made in The USA. Two capsules every morning. I have read their papers myself, which is more than most of my customers do. Here, you can take it alongside whatever you take and write your number every morning. Your son does not trust words. He trusts numbers. Bring him a 100 of them. He told me to bring you numbers, not words. 139, 131, 124. Slept through. Bonsai. Walk to the market with Emmy. Mochi one zero one. The mochi was an experiment. You wrote it down every morning. Every morning. You trained me well. Eight weeks. Eight weeks. It fits the page. What is in it? Show me. Real Ceylon. Real buburine. Tested by an outside lab made in The USA. What does it do, dad? I will use Ono san's words. Your insulin still works. Your cells stopped answering it. The cinnamon helps them answer again. That part I know is true. But on its own, the cinnamon only gets you halfway. Berberine helps it dissolve and reach your cells, and it activates AMPK, the switch that decides burn or store. Two ingredients, two halves of the same problem. I have heard both of those names. People bring them up all the time. I never thought to look in a spice shop. That is where the spices are. And your pills? Every morning, exactly as before. Nothing changed there. Good. Keep it that way. You always told me numbers do not lie. I did. Dad, I am sorry I made you feel you could not tell me. You worry because you love me. I always knew that. Eat. It is still warm. It is so good. Uncle is eating pasta. Whatever you are doing, keep doing it. I intend to. Adios. For two months, I kept it from my son because I was sure he would take my dinner away. My son only ever wanted me at this table for many more Sundays. If someone you love worries about what is on your plate, show them your numbers instead of arguing about the cake. I order it online now. It saves me the walk to Ono san's shop, though I still go for the tea. Real Ceylon, real berberine, tested by an outside lab made in The USA. There's a thirty day money back guarantee. There's a sale running right now. If you wanna get both and you can still see this link, that means they haven't sold out yet. Link's below.\",\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://resilia.shop/products/resilia-ceylon-cinnamon\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"resilia.shop\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Explore the Power of Ceylon Cinnamon Today!\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":null,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":null,\"duplicates\":28,\"reachDelta1d\":null,\"reachDelta7d\":null,\"reachDelta30d\":null},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":null,\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":24,\"currentRank\":24,\"rankDelta\":-13,\"improvementPct\":10},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1100961186080202\",\"collationId\":\"1686235706468000\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-13T22:01:47.337Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-11-13T08:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-26T07:39:22.539Z\",\"daysRunning\":14,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/8dd9e9f8bb2e4e12e8b34d2a89503aaf5a48e7f6560dbde591673f911b758ce7.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/ec1fb1571227f5a26ae4d0d986239ee1a562e631380fb15e87ea2219379c073f.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1050252671500385\",\"name\":\"Dr. Matthew Walker\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1050252671500385.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1050252671500385\",\"liveAdsCount\":1106,\"reach30d\":805188,\"totalReach\":1927191,\"countriesCount\":4,\"facebookLikes\":4501,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Looking to Support Healthy Blood Sugar Naturally? 🌿\\n\\nExperience the Power of Metabolae Sri Lankan Ceylon Cinnamon!\\n\\n✅ Helps support healthy blood sugar levels\\n✅ Supports steady daily energy\\n✅ Helps reduce blood sugar crashes\\n✅ Authentic Sri Lankan Ceylon cinnamon\\n✅ 200+ Clinical studies\\n✅ Enhanced with MCT oil for absorption\\n\\nSupport healthier glucose metabolism naturally with research-backed ingredients designed for daily stability.\",\"transcript\":\"People take Ceylon cinnamon for their heart, completely unaware of the biological domino effect. Once that toxic plaque stops choking your blood flow, your liver, your kidneys, your prostate, and your eyes literally come back to life. I said it's great for your heart, but it's good for so much more. Forget 50 different supplements for 50 different things, and listen to me very carefully. Just focus on getting true Ceylon cinnamon. Cassia cinnamon from China, the kind sitting on every grocery store shelf, is not the same as true Ceylon cinnamon from Sri Lanka. The cassia stuff is a completely different tree with almost none of the active compounds, and it carries coumarin that may actually damage your liver. Now you might ask, why does one bark help your heart and everything else? Because every organ in your body is fed by blood vessels, and those vessels all get attacked by the same two things: trapped sugar grinding through the lining, and the oxidative stress that comes with it. That's the root of most problems in the body. Ceylon cinnamon carries two compounds that hit both. MHC P opens the doors on your cells, so the sugar stops staying trapped and grinding through your vessels. Cinnamaldehyde is one of the most powerful natural antioxidants ever studied for vascular tissue. It gets inside the vessel lining and neutralizes exactly that oxidative damage. As you age, your vessels may carry years of this damage that quietly affects how well your heart, your liver, your kidneys, and your prostate all work, because they all run on the same blood supply. Remember, Ceylon cinnamon may help clear the trapped sugar and neutralize the free radicals behind that oxidative load, which may help support your body's natural defenses, support healthy blood flow to every organ, and help support the kind of body you used to take for granted. But before you go buy any cinnamon mixed with fillers, to know your cinnamon is real and potent, it should be true Ceylon, DNA verified at the species level, so you know it's not cassia, suspended in MCT oil so the fat-soluble compounds actually absorb, third-party tested here in the United States, and dosed at the full 7,200 milligram used in the actual research. Metabole meets that standard with every batch. Each soft gel delivers true Ceylon cinnamon from Sri Lanka, concentrated 12 to 1, suspended in coconut MCT oil, nothing else. Thousands of pouches move while stock lasts. Tap the link below.\",\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://metabolae.com/products/softgels-ceylon\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"metabolae.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg Equivalent with MCT Oil\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":3853,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":35,\"duplicates\":28,\"reachDelta1d\":383,\"reachDelta7d\":2069,\"reachDelta30d\":3612},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"AU\",\"CA\",\"GB\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":103,\"currentRank\":103,\"rankDelta\":4,\"improvementPct\":9.31},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1353595290240209\",\"collationId\":\"1422441006609351\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-29T05:25:33.241Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-07-28T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-08-02T04:01:36.597Z\",\"daysRunning\":122,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/a0830e05ca76b8bddb71a3b3650f31520d544eb5caf872cd14861e993e99a73a.png\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1013442788524883\",\"name\":\"Caroline Moore\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1013442788524883.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1013442788524883\",\"liveAdsCount\":3389,\"reach30d\":1144134,\"totalReach\":2517956,\"countriesCount\":5,\"facebookLikes\":1884,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Please don't buy this cinnamon. I was diagnosed with type 2 six months ago. A1C 7.1. Here's what happened when I took Metabolae for 30 days .\\n\\nI'm Caroline Moore. I've been a diabetes educator for 22 years. I teach type 2 patients how to check their glucose, count their carbs, take their metformin, and accept that they'll be on the meds for the rest of their lives.\\n\\nSix months ago I sat in an exam room and heard my own doctor say the same words I've said to hundreds of patients. Your A1C came back at 7.1. We're going to start you on metformin. This is manageable.\\n\\nShe handed me the prescription. I filled it. The bottle has been sitting on my counter, unopened, for six months.\\n\\nI couldn't do it. Not yet. I've spent 22 years watching type 2 patients follow every instruction and watch their numbers climb anyway. Metformin at 40. Blood pressure medication at 44. Statin at 47. By 55 they're on four drugs and their kidneys are starting to slip. I know the trajectory. I teach the trajectory. I wasn't ready to walk it.\\n\\nA colleague at a continuing education conference mentioned Metabolae. She said her mother's A1C dropped a full point in ninety days. Ceylon cinnamon, not Cassia. Concentrated 12:1 and suspended in MCT oil so it actually absorbs. I'd heard the cinnamon claims for years and dismissed them all — because every study I'd read used a specific species, dose, and delivery that no supplement on Amazon was actually shipping.\\n\\nI figured I had nothing to lose. The metformin bottle would still be on the counter if this didn't work.\\n\\nDay 1: One softgel with breakfast. Didn't expect anything.\\n\\nDay 3: I checked my fasting glucose. 156. Not what I wanted but 20 points below my usual morning read of 178. Tested again. 154. I didn't say anything to my husband.\\n\\nDay 5: 148. Three days in a row under 160. That hadn't happened since the diagnosis.\\n\\nDay 7: I slept through the night. First time in months. I'd blamed the diagnosis stress. Turns out it was the 3am cortisol spike from a liver still overproducing glucose. Nobody told me that in any of my training.\\n\\nDay 10: 138. I stopped dreading my morning finger pricks. For 22 years I've told patients the meter is not a report card. This week I finally believed it about my own.\\n\\nDay 14: The afternoon crashes stopped. The 2pm wall I'd been coffee-medicating my way through disappeared. Steady all day.\\n\\nDay 17: My cravings loosened. The bread-and-sugar pull I've been telling patients was normal for insulin resistance — gone. Not managed. Gone.\\n\\nDay 21: Fasting glucose 118. I tested twice. My husband was watching. He didn't say anything. He just put his hand on my shoulder. He's been carrying the diagnosis with me for six months.\\n\\nDay 24: I ate pasta for dinner. Real pasta. With bread. First time since the diagnosis. Tested two hours later expecting the worst. 132. That used to be my fasting.\\n\\nDay 27: Slept through the night again. Every night that week.\\n\\nDay 30: Fasting glucose 108. I sat on the edge of the bed and stared at the meter. Six months ago I was 178. Today I was 108.\\n\\n108.\\n\\nMy husband came in and saw my face. What's wrong?\\n\\nI showed him the meter.\\n\\nHe started crying.\\n\\nSix weeks after I started, I went back for bloodwork. A1C came back at 5.6.\\n\\nShe pulled up my chart. Looked at me. What did you change?\\n\\nI told her about Metabolae. About the species, the dose, the MCT oil suspension.\\n\\nShe made a note. Then she said something I wasn't expecting. Whatever this is, keep doing it. We're going to want to reconsider what we called this at your next appointment.\\n\\nThe metformin bottle is still sitting on my counter. Unopened. Six months old.\\n\\nI'm furious.\\n\\nI'm furious because I've spent 22 years teaching patients that type 2 is a management condition. That metformin is for life. That the number is the enemy and the meter is the report card. And nobody at any conference in any of those years told me about the species, the dose, the delivery.\\n\\nHere's what I learned.\\n\\nMost cinnamon supplements aren't Ceylon. They're Cassia — a different species with up to 250 times more coumarin, which can damage the liver at supplement doses. The clinical studies that showed real blood sugar benefits used true Ceylon cinnamon. Cinnamomum verum.\\n\\nMost are underdosed. The studies used concentrated extract equivalent to 6,000-7,200mg daily. Most capsules have 500-1,500mg of powder.\\n\\nMost use dry powder that doesn't absorb. Cinnamon's active compounds are fat-soluble. Without a fat carrier they pass right through you. That's why Metabolae is suspended in MCT oil.\\n\\nTrue Ceylon. 7,200mg equivalent. MCT oil suspension. Third-party tested. GMP certified.\\n\\n90-day money-back guarantee. If your numbers don't move, you pay nothing. No hassle. No paperwork.\\n\\nOne softgel with breakfast. That's all I did.\\n\\nSo don't buy it. There will be more for me. Hopefully they don't sell out again — the buy two get one free deal is what got me here, and I'd like it to still be there when I reorder.\\n\\nIf your A1C just crossed the line. If your doctor just handed you a prescription. If the bottle is sitting on your counter and you're not ready to open it. If you were told this is manageable and something in you refuses to accept that management is the whole story.\\n\\nTry this. Track your fasting glucose every morning. Give it 30 days.\\n\\nI went from 7.1 to 5.6. From newly diagnosed to my doctor asking to reconsider the diagnosis.\\n\\nThe metformin bottle is still unopened.\\n\\n~ Caroline Moore\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://metabolae.com/pages/lp-pd1-cc-wh-bloodsugar-b\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"metabolae.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg Equivalent with MCT Oil\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":\"Metabolae\"},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":11089,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":100,\"duplicates\":28,\"reachDelta1d\":110,\"reachDelta7d\":2257,\"reachDelta30d\":4632},\"audience\":{\"targetedCo