thing we sell. Everybody says the same thing. Then give me all of it, whatever it takes. I bought the most expensive things on that shelf. Every morning, every night, a full week. And by Sunday, my face was worse than when I started, hungrier, more tired, and still gray. I sat on the edge of the tub and I thought, that's it then. This is just what I look like now. Gary walked out on me two years ago, told me I'd given up on myself. Sound familiar? Lorraine, you remember what I looked like that year? This is what changed it. What is this? A pouch of cinnamon? Real Ceylon cinnamon and berberine from Sri Lanka, not the cassia from China that's in every grocery store. The cassia strains your liver and does nothing for you. This one has a compound called cenamaldehyde. It opens the receptors on your cells back up so the sugar you eat has somewhere to go beside your waste in your face. Carmen, I've tried everything. The counter, the gummies, the most expensive stuff they had. Lorraine, I'm 63. Everybody at my work thinks I'm 45. Nobody believes me. And this is the only thing I take. There's about three weeks left in that pouch. Two capsules every single morning. Don't skip one. Oh, this is nonsense. But I took two with my coffee the next morning. Twenty minutes later, something I hadn't felt in years. My head was clear, not caffeine clear, different, steady. By three in the afternoon, I was still steady, no crash, no reaching for the fridge. The afternoon fog was gone. The pull towards sugar was gone. By day four, I woke up and my face wasn't puffy. The grayness I'd been living with was lifting. One side of my face was the woman he walked away from. The other side was me at 40. There I was. That evening at 06:30, I checked in the car mirror. The puffiness hadn't come back. The bags under my eyes were softer. By week one, I told myself it couldn't be two capsules because my whole body felt different. Lighter, warmer, awake. The gray was gone. It had been working on my cells the whole time I'd given up on them. Three weeks in, and Carmen's pouch was empty. The divorce papers came Tuesday. Nobody called anymore. Some days I barely spoke. Carmen, where do I get it? I'll send you the link. Recilia, real Ceylon cinnamon from Sri Lanka with berberine. One thousand milligrams of Ceylon, five hundred milligrams of berberine. Two capsules every morning. Made for women past 50. Thirty day guarantee, give me six. Two days later, it arrived. The party was a week away. Finally, I was ready for something. Almost a month on it now. And the night before my mother's dinner, I laid a red dress on the bed. First time since March, I wasn't dreading a room, and the dress fit the way it used to. You're ready and you look amazing. Oh, look at my daughter. Oh, baby. Where did you find that face? That's the one I raised. Happy birthday, mama. Lorraine, what did you do? Half this wowed is staring at you. Lorraine, you look beautiful. You look genuinely beautiful. I said you were tired. I'm sorry for what I said to you that night. I shouldn't have said any of it. She's only 90 once. Dennis, let's give her a good picture. Everybody in. Lorraine, you stay right here next to me. Okay. Out with it. Your mother thinks you've met somebody. Two capsules in the morning. That's it, that's it. I bought six. That one's yours. Denise asked me twice last year if I was sick. Twice, Beverly. Mom, I saw them back in March. What? Her car outside his office. I never told you I thought it would break you. And then a few weeks ago, I stopped being frightened for you. That's how I knew you were back. Come Sunday, I'm cooking. Two weeks on that stuff, and my husband won't let me leave the house without him. You look brand new. And listen, they stand behind it. Thirty days. If you don't see it, you don't pay a cent. I checked before I ordered more. I don't trust anybody's promises. Oh my gosh. In here. Food's on. It's called Resilia, real Ceylon cinnamon from Sri Lanka with berberine, not the cassia from China that strains your liver and does nothing. This one has cinnamaldehyne that opens your cell doors back up and berberine that flips the switch to burn the stored sugar instead of holding it in your face. One thousand milligrams of Ceylon, five hundred milligrams of berberine, two capsules every morning. That's it. It works on your cells the whole day. Six weeks ago, my husband told me I was a woman who'd given up. That woman doesn't live at this address. It's up to 70% off right now. Thirty day guarantee and the link's underneath.","callToAction":"LEARN MORE","landingPageUrl":"https://resilia.shop/products/resilia-ceylon-cinnamon","landingPageDomain":"resilia.shop","ctaDescription":"Explore the Power of Ceylon Cinnamon Today!","ctaLinkDescription":null},"metrics":{"reach":null,"aggregatedReach":null,"estimatedSpend":null,"duplicates":32,"reachDelta1d":null,"reachDelta7d":null,"reachDelta30d":null},"audience":{"targetedCountries":["US"],"mainCountry":null,"gender":null,"ageMin":null,"ageMax":null},"rank":{"positionInPage":4,"currentRank":4,"rankDelta":0,"improvementPct":1.67},"flags":{"isEuAd":null,"isLowReach":false,"isMediaChanged":true,"hasPartnerBadge":false}},{"id":"facebook_1083126674716971","collationId":"1442317558075295","platform":"facebook","status":"inactive","createdAt":"2026-10-23T12:29:27.375Z","firstSeenAt":"2026-10-22T07:00:00.000Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-11-04T02:09:34.322Z","daysRunning":13,"media":{"type":"image","thumbnailUrl":null,"mediaUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/4b50c8269b488ae983f4dd0baf253fa41267e88fe9fe849eacd57660bce3f0f2.jpg"},"advertiser":{"id":"1163931893470874","name":"Beating Blood Sugar Together","logoUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1163931893470874.jpg","facebookPageId":"1163931893470874","liveAdsCount":7,"reach30d":1709,"totalReach":19597,"countriesCount":6,"facebookLikes":54,"instagramFollowers":142},"content":{"title":null,"body":"Tried berberine before and it either